ge because there's really  no reason there never should be someone  who dies making a film i think that  it'll definitely be looked at and there  are ways that you can mitigate the the  risk  by doing it in post-production  by changing the shooting angle it's been  reported that before thursday's incident  several crew members had walked off the  set of rust over safety concerns  including misfires of a prop gun  the movie's producers say they weren't  made aware of any official complaints  concerning weapon or prop safety but  they would review procedures safety they  said was their top priority  there are still so many questions over  an incident that to many was unthinkable  one that's left an industry shaken and a  family grieving a loss they describe as  enormous greg milam sky news los angeles
 

